      "title": "Interview #106 Jeff Radke, CEO, Accelerant Holdings",
      "summary": "Jeff Radke, CEO of Accelerant Holdings, breaks down why insurance pricing should stay deterministic even as AI takes on more of the work, so the same risk with the same facts always gets the same price. He explains why policy systems built when storage was expensive kept so few facts that a zip code and an address used up two of them, how AI acts as the canary in the coal mine that tells machine learning where to look, and how models found Liverpool pubs south of the river outperforming those to the north based on which football club locals supported. Jeff also dives into who owns the error when an AI agent mislabels a building before an underwriter ever opens the file, and why big insurers' decades of data lose out to inertia and personal spreadsheets. Finally, he shares how agents may have to recreate the apprenticeship junior underwriters are losing, and why AI is so cheap it brings tears to your eyes. Free AI lessons for leaders, built on these interviews: https://tonyphoang.com/learn Be a guest on the show: https://tonyphoang.com/guest Live interviews at your conference: https://tonyphoang.com/live Music and credits: https://tonyphoang.com/credits",
